    {
      "id": "cmx2yoa",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "NATIONAL INCOME"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "National Income represents the total monetary value of all final goods and services produced within a nation in a given period.",
        "Inflation in India is monitored using the Consumer Price Index (CPI) and Wholesale Price Index (WPI).",
        "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) regulates liquidity using instruments such as Repo Rate, Reverse Repo Rate, CRR, and SLR.",
        "Fiscal Policy manages government revenues, taxation, and expenditures to control public debt and fiscal deficit.",
        "The Human Development Index (HDI) assesses progress across health, education, and decent standard of living."
      ],
      "id": "jo08uvk"
    },
